{"title":"Root (operation)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th <b>root</b> of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d35112ae0400463779b8c3320f3bc597d81374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, is a common operation on numbers and a partial <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inverse\" title=\"Inverse\">inverse</a> to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponentiation\" title=\"Exponentiation\">exponentiation</a>. (The proper inverse is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm\" title=\"Logarithm\">logarithm</a>)\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#How_to_compute_all_the_roots_of\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">How to compute all the roots of</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Example_with_a_real_number\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example with a real number</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#How_to_approximate_a_root\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">How to approximate a root</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any (not necessarily real) numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae68eee38785d2a0ddee59a13e4e1d5f951a30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9962081cf8b6e34039528449be2773a54b04cf8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sqrt[n]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e936b6935e7fe275eae81009115c1cad110c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^n=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Note that we generally take only the positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, if we wish to take both the positive and negative roots, we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663f9e8b75a5e424090d648fb042a266557b4538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm\\sqrt[n]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_compute_all_the_roots_of\">How to compute all the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d35112ae0400463779b8c3320f3bc597d81374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: How to compute all the roots of\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A known method to compute all the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d35112ae0400463779b8c3320f3bc597d81374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> is by the DeMoivre's formula.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403252c1db55643424ba7299c1bea43e0a412aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{x}=\\sqrt[n]{|x|}\\left(\\cos\\frac{\\theta+2\\pi k}{n}+i\\sin\\frac{\\theta+2\\pi k}{n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"333\" height=\"43\" /> , where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/72604d7ff49fcffc7b594254ea680d02597a5f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,...,n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2526e68dc22238167460a9af88bd375490b77b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSee that in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a2c8ef17e980728e19b4a41cc616d6de385d93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{|x|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" /> we compute its principal root.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_with_a_real_number\">Example with a real number</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Example with a real number\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute all the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37768646439e8577eb90ffffdd1f5e1b492972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^4-16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd>First, we need to rearrange the equation .</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0653364fbe8f7466329ed0ed72ead5976bd1d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\sqrt[4]{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>See that here the \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />\" would be the number 16.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>Then, we compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0b5be98f956a5a8fb38971c0c7d4e6bead93cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|16|=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>As 2 is a pure real number, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/422d8671db62ffe3adc0d7dff74aa73630061d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d164dd51c4a3ba53fcdd187c7bf57522ce6b3434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>We separately compute the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d164dd51c4a3ba53fcdd187c7bf57522ce6b3434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763fa9652dc1c3f8b9dc32c7dc0dc0edb16feaa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{16}=\\sqrt[4]{16}\\left(\\cos\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot0}{4}+i\\sin\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot0}{4}\\right)\\implies\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"431\" height=\"43\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50c9d2dbc3c0dd36143c8abdd2fdfe075a78993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{16}=\\sqrt[4]{16}\\left(\\cos\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot1}{4}+i\\sin\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot1}{4}\\right)\\implies\\boxed{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"439\" height=\"45\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055ad37a87fa2fd13570a8ec030d818b9c2e81c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{16}=\\sqrt[4]{16}\\left(\\cos\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot2}{4}+i\\sin\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot2}{4}\\right)\\implies\\boxed{-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"447\" height=\"45\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f764f8e931a75f70d94b2752567ac637da7f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{16}=\\sqrt[4]{16}\\left(\\cos\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot3}{4}+i\\sin\\frac{0+2\\pi\\cdot3}{4}\\right)\\implies\\boxed{-2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"451\" height=\"43\" /></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_approximate_a_root\">How to approximate a root</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: How to approximate a root\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There's many methods to approximate roots. Here are two:\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbae9fbc9590f5179fb3c25fc262dadca40c86b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x}\\approx\\frac{x+x_0}{2\\sqrt{x_0}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is the nearest perfect square.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Computing the square root of 5,</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>We know that the nearest perfect square is 4, so,</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f9ac3cfbca534a6e62eaf9397efa90d48adeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}\\approx\\frac{5+4}{2\\sqrt{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"95\" height=\"43\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7aeff01415425518306b589c3b502fe0909da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}\\approx2.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>With this method you can get a little good approximation. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b18063863263890f4766b4d6cca6d4b7e5b4427.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}\\simeq2.2360679$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Also, you can use Newton-Raphson's method:</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7605fa37d34d6898fd46697d2ed785e3c1ea85cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=x_n-\\frac{f(x_n)}{f&#39;(x_n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" /> , where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a number close to the root.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>The more times you apply this formula (consecutively), the better is the approximation that you can get.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>Computing the square root of 2,</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>See that it would be:</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db1f87c7de444f61b4aa1184aeae8678599199c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1226014633b93a4af77c1b358235a130ee6be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-2=0$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45ce2559f89245764a2b8630ff0ce18c70e21328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(x)=x^2-2}\\implies f&#39;(x)=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"253\" height=\"31\" /></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/646611eb8dadcdcb79060fc1f6d5ca0e6bac97b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1.4-\\frac{1.4^2-2}{2\\cdot1.4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"39\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6ab94a2c2467f6c31864dd0fc34670ac8aec4df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1.4142857142857144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>This it's very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. Sometimes it can be a \"very ugly bashing\", but it's a method to get really good approximations. But, if couldn't get a good approximation at first, you can apply it a second time.</dd></dl>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root\" title=\"Square root\">Square root</a>, a special form of a root.</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105353\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 217/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 289/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7775/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.388      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.388      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5850:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018105353 and revision id 122677. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}